<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

  <!-- Converted from the in-game custom xenotype, originally saved as
       "Achonion Sanguophage". Baked into a def rather than loaded from a local
       .xtp file so that it is byte-identical on every client - a hard
       requirement for multiplayer.

       Genes marked [ARCHITE] have biostatArc > 0, which means VQE Ancients'
       archite injection system can also grant them later. See README. -->
  <XenotypeDef>
    <defName>Archinity_ArchonianSanguophage</defName>
    <label>archonian sanguophage</label>
    <iconPath>UI/Icons/Xenotypes/Custom/CustomXenotypeIcon5</iconPath>
    <inheritable>false</inheritable>
    <canGenerateAsCombatant>false</canGenerateAsCombatant>
    <factionlessGenerationWeight>0</factionlessGenerationWeight>
    <combatPowerFactor>2.5</combatPowerFactor>
    <displayPriority>500</displayPriority>
    <description>Something reached backwards through time and touched a handful of neolithic humans.\n\nThe archons do not explain themselves. What they left behind were creatures that do not age, do not scar, and do not stay dead - wearing plasteel under their skin and carrying archite machinery in blood they cannot produce for themselves.\n\nThey woke among people who had no word for what they were, and were worshipped for it. They remember nothing of the touch. They only know that they are unfinished, and that the thing which made them is still out there, further up.</description>
    <descriptionShort>Ageless, deathless archite-tainted immortals. Effectively unkillable in a fair fight and incapable of reproducing, they must drink human blood to survive and are permanently psychologically unstable. Every gene they carry points toward something they have not become yet.</descriptionShort>
    <genes>

      <!-- Archite frame: ageless, deathless, self-repairing -->
      <li>Ageless</li>                                                          <!-- [ARCHITE] -->
      <li>Deathless</li>                                                        <!-- [ARCHITE] -->
      <li>DiseaseFree</li>                                                      <!-- [ARCHITE] -->
      <li>PerfectImmunity</li>                                                  <!-- [ARCHITE] -->
      <li>TotalHealing</li>                                                     <!-- [ARCHITE] -->
      <li>Coagulate</li>
      <li MayRequire="vanillaquestsexpanded.ancients">VQEA_Woundless</li>            <!-- [ARCHITE] -->
      <li MayRequire="vanillaquestsexpanded.ancients">VQEA_SelfRepairingTissue</li>  <!-- [ARCHITE] -->
      <li MayRequire="vanillaquestsexpanded.ancients">VQEA_PlasteelSkin</li>         <!-- [ARCHITE] -->
      <li MayRequire="vanillaquestsexpanded.ancients">VQEA_Herculean</li>            <!-- [ARCHITE] -->
      <li MayRequire="vanillaquestsexpanded.ancients">VQEA_PerfectVision</li>        <!-- [ARCHITE] -->
      <li MayRequire="vanillaquestsexpanded.ancients">VQEA_BlurRunner</li>           <!-- [ARCHITE] -->
      <li>LongjumpLegs</li>
      <li>Neversleep</li>
      <li MayRequire="ludeon.rimworld.odyssey">VacuumResistance_Total</li>       <!-- [ARCHITE] -->

      <!-- Hemogenic dependency: the price of the gift.

           NO DEATHREST, deliberately. Every sanguophage in the world must
           periodically go into the ground; these two never do. That absence is
           what separates the founders from anyone they later convert - vanilla
           sanguophages already get Deathless and Ageless, so those cannot be
           the distinction. Archinity.Altar's reimplant patch ADDS Deathrest to
           every convert, so the asymmetry holds no matter how many are made. -->
      <li>Hemogenic</li>
      <li>Bloodfeeder</li>
      <li MayRequire="vanillaracesexpanded.sanguophage">VRE_Hemosmosis</li>
      <li MayRequire="vanillaracesexpanded.sanguophage">VRE_LowHemogenDrain</li>
      <li MayRequire="vanillaracesexpanded.sanguophage">VRE_AnimalFeeder</li>

      <!-- Propagation: they cannot breed, and for a long time cannot convert.

           XenogermReimplanter is REMOVED from the start. Two chosen ones who
           can mint copies of themselves at will are not chosen. For roughly
           400 days there is no way at all to share what they are - until the
           Descent Engine quest returns the gene in the Industrial era, gated
           on Xenogermination, at the exact moment the colony understands what
           it has been doing. That beat only exists because the gene was taken
           away first. -->
      <li>Sterile</li>

      <!-- Costs -->
      <li MayRequire="vanillaracesexpanded.waster">VRE_Instability_Extreme</li>

      <!-- Presentation -->
      <li>Beauty_Beautiful</li>
      <li>Aggression_DeadCalm</li>
      <li>Voice_Human</li>
      <li>Body_Standard</li>
      <li>Skin_LightGray</li>
      <li>Hair_SnowWhite</li>
      <li>ElongatedFingers</li>
      <li MayRequire="vanillaracesexpanded.sanguophage">VRE_SanguineHair</li>
      <li MayRequire="vanillaracesexpanded.saurid">VRESaurids_Pheromones</li>

    </genes>
  </XenotypeDef>

</Defs>
